{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Dist","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Star.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Basic"],"declarations":51,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.not_in_failure_locus_iff_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.not_in_failure_locus_iff_generic","kind":"theorem","line":405,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L405-L414","doc":"A `q` outside the failure locus is generic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.failureLocus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.failureLocus","kind":"def","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L394-L403","doc":"The **exact failure locus** of generic-q Wedderburn / Baer-*:\n`{q : ∃ k ∈ [2, n], q^{2k} = 1}`. At each such `q`, the\nquantum integer `[k]_q := (q^k - q^{-k}) / (q - q^{-1})`\nvanishes for some `k ≤ n`, the Hoefsmit projector becomes\nsingular, and the Jacobson radical is non-trivial.\n\nCo-located with the Volume Conjecture asymptotic regime\n(`rem:vc-as-depth-2-instance`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.bar_central_idempotent_transpose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.bar_central_idempotent_transpose","kind":"theorem","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L381-L390","doc":"Bar involution acts on central idempotents by partition\ntranspose: `star (e_λ) = e_{λ'}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.bar_centralIdempotent_transpose_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.bar_centralIdempotent_transpose_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L368-L379","doc":"**External axiom** (manuscript §prop:explicit-central-idempotent\n\"Cross-checks\" §3-4): the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` acts on\ncentral idempotents by partition transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.partitionTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.partitionTranspose","kind":"def","line":349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L349-L366","doc":"Transpose of a partition (Young-diagram conjugate).  For each\ncolumn index `j` (0-indexed up to the row length of the first\nrow), the transposed partition's `j`-th entry is the number of\noriginal rows with at least `j + 1` boxes.  Examples:\n\n  `transpose [3, 1] = [2, 1, 1]`  (Young diagram with 3 + 1 = 4 boxes)\n  `transpose [2, 2] = [2, 2]`     (self-conjugate)\n  `transpose [4]    = [1, 1, 1, 1]`\n\nPer Gemini PR #634 review: replaces the previous incorrect\n`List.reverse` placeholder.  Reversal does NOT yield the\ntranspose (e.g. `[3, 1].reverse = [1, 3]` which is not even a\nvalid partition; the correct transpose is `[2, 1, 1]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.central_idempotent_orthogonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.central_idempotent_orthogonal","kind":"theorem","line":340,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L340-L347","doc":"Central idempotents are orthogonal idempotents:\n`e_λ · e_μ = δ_{λμ} · e_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.centralIdempotent_orthogonal_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.centralIdempotent_orthogonal_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L329-L338","doc":"**External axiom**: orthogonality of central idempotents follows\nfrom Lagrange interpolation in commuting variables (the JM\nelements pairwise commute by [murphy1981]). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.central_idempotent_central","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.central_idempotent_central","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L320-L327","doc":"Central idempotents are central: `e_λ · x = x · e_λ` for all\n`x ∈ H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.centralIdempotent_central_axiom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.centralIdempotent_central_axiom","kind":"axiom","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L304-L318","doc":"**External axiom (Murphy 1981; Dipper–James 1986):**\n\nCentral idempotents are central via the Lagrange-interpolation\nconstruction in commuting JM elements.  Recorded as an axiom\n(§3b-cond pattern) since concrete proof requires constructing\nJM elements + interpolation polynomial, both of which depend on\na full IwahoriHeckeAlgebra implementation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.centralIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.centralIdempotent","kind":"opaque","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L297-L302","doc":"The **central primitive idempotent** `e_λ` for partition\n`λ ⊢ n`. Constructed via Lagrange interpolation in JM elements\nper `prop:explicit-central-idempotent`.  Opaque, not a placeholder\n`def` — see the note above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.jucysMurphy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.jucysMurphy","kind":"opaque","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L290-L295","doc":"The **Jucys–Murphy element** `J_k` of `H_n(q)`. Definition uses\nthe formula `J_k = q^{1-k} Σ_{i < k} σ_{i, k}` from\n`prop:jucys-murphy-central-elements-qou`.  Opaque, not a placeholder\n`def` — see the note above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.wedderburn_decomposition_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.wedderburn_decomposition_generic","kind":"def","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L231-L258","doc":"**Wedderburn decomposition at generic q** (named conditional conjecture,\n§3b).  When `q` is generic, `H_n(q)` is finite-dimensional semisimple over\n`R` and decomposes as a direct sum of matrix algebras indexed by the\npartitions `λ ⊢ n` (here ranged over by the supplied list `parts`).\n\nHonest disposition: the decomposition is *named* as a `Prop` over the\nopaque carrier — it asserts the existence of a complete family of pairwise\northogonal central idempotents `{e_λ}` that sum to `1` (the Wedderburn unit\nresolution).  This is the structural content of semisimplicity; the proof\nneeds Mathlib's matrix-algebra / seminormal-form infrastructure and is the\nopen part (`prop:wedderburn-weight-canonical`, `prop:hoefsmit-seminormal-form`).\nReplaces the previous `: True := trivial` (vacuous) projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.IsGeneric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.IsGeneric","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L225-L229","doc":"The \"generic\" condition on `q`: `q^{2k} ≠ 1` for `k ∈ {2, …, n}`.\nThis is the precise locus on which `H_n(q)` is semisimple\n(`prop:hecke-baer-star-generic` failure-locus characterisation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.markovTrace_stab_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.markovTrace_stab_comm","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L204-L221","doc":"**Consumer (the two Markov moves compose).**  Cyclicity of `tr_{M, n+1}`\nlets the stabilisation move be read in either order: the Markov trace of the\nnew generator times an included element equals `z · tr_{M, n}` regardless of\nside.  A genuine derivation from the two axioms — `MarkovTraceStabilisation`\nis not decorative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceStabilisation.stabilisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceStabilisation.stabilisation","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L196-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceStabilisation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceStabilisation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L192-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceStabilisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceStabilisation","kind":"class","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L180-L200","doc":"Markov trace stabilisation: with the tower inclusion `incl : H_n ↪ H_{n+1}`\n(`HeckeInclusion`) and the new top generator `σ_n` of `H_{n+1}` (index `n-1`\nof its `Fin n` generators), the Markov trace satisfies\n\n`tr_{M, n+1}(incl a · σ_n) = z · tr_{M, n}(a)`\n\nfor the Markov parameter `z : R` (concretely `z = 1 / (q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`,\ncarried here as an abstract `R`-parameter since `q^{1/2}` need not lie in a\ngeneric `R`).  Together with `MarkovTraceCyclic` this is the defining pair of\nMarkov moves characterising `tr_M` (Jones 1987 §3).  `hn : 0 < n` makes the\n`σ_n` index `⟨n-1, _⟩ : Fin n` well-formed (stabilisation adds `σ_n` to\n`H_n`, which requires `n ≥ 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.map_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.map_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L177-L177","doc":"The inclusion preserves generators: `σ_i ↦ σ_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.map_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.map_mul","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L172-L172","doc":"The inclusion is multiplicative (a ring hom). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.map_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.map_one","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L167-L167","doc":"The inclusion is unital. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.incl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.incl","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L165-L165","doc":"The underlying inclusion of carriers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeInclusion","kind":"class","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L157-L178","doc":"**Tower inclusion** `H_n ↪ H_{n+1}`: the unital ring hom that sends each\nbraid generator `σ_i` of `H_n` to the same-indexed generator of `H_{n+1}`,\nrealising `H_n` as the subalgebra of `H_{n+1}` on the first `n-1` strands.\nThe Markov stabilisation move is stated against this map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceCyclic.cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceCyclic.cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceCyclic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceCyclic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L151-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceCyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.MarkovTraceCyclic","kind":"class","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L150-L155","doc":"Markov trace cyclicity: `tr_M(a · b) = tr_M(b · a)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar.bar_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar.bar_q","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L142-L142","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar.bar_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar.bar_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L137-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar.mk","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBar","kind":"class","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L134-L146","doc":"The bar involution `* : σ_i ↦ σ_i⁻¹` is the standard antipode\nstructure on `H_n(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeFarCommute.far_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeFarCommute.far_commute","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeFarCommute.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeFarCommute.mk","kind":"ctor","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L126-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeFarCommute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeFarCommute","kind":"class","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L125-L130","doc":"Far commutativity: `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i - j| ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBraid.braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBraid.braid","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L117-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBraid.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBraid.mk","kind":"ctor","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L116-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBraid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeBraid","kind":"class","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L115-L123","doc":"The braid relation: `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeQuadratic.quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeQuadratic.quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeQuadratic.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeQuadratic.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeQuadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeQuadratic","kind":"class","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L105-L113","doc":"The quadratic Hecke relation: `(σ_i - q)(σ_i + q⁻¹) = 0`, with `q⁻¹`\nthe `IsUnit`-natural inverse `↑(h_unit.unit)⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom.scalarOf_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom.scalarOf_one","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom.scalarOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom.scalarOf","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom.mk","kind":"ctor","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.HeckeRingHom","kind":"class","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L97-L103","doc":"Algebra hom from `R` to the Hecke-algebra carrier — provides\nthe scalar embedding required to write `(q : R) ↪ H.carrier`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.instNonemptyCarrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.instNonemptyCarrier","kind":"instance","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L71-L78","doc":"`H.carrier` is nonempty: it carries a `Ring` (the `ring` field), hence\nhas `0`.  Registered so `opaque`/placeholder constants valued in\n`H.carrier` (`jucysMurphy`, `centralIdempotent`) elaborate (an `opaque`\nconstant of type `T` requires `Nonempty T`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.markov_trace","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Markov trace as an `R`-linear map `carrier → R`.  Linearity,\nMarkov-trace cyclicity, and the stabilisation property are\nplaced as separate axioms below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.sigma","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The braid generators `σ_i` for `i ∈ Fin (n - 1)`. Defined\nonly when `n ≥ 1`; trivial otherwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.star_ring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.star_ring","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Star (bar involution) structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.ring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.ring","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Algebra structure on the carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.carrier","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The underlying carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.IwahoriHeckeAPI.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/IwahoriHeckeAPI.lean#L34-L65","doc":"The **Iwahori–Hecke algebra** `H_n(q)` of type `A_{n-1}` over a\ncommutative ring `R` with invertible element `q ∈ R^×`. The\nalgebra has braid generators `σ_i` (`i = 1, …, n - 1`) satisfying:\n\n1. *Quadratic relation* `(σ_i - q)(σ_i + q⁻¹) = 0`;\n2. *Braid relation* `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`;\n3. *Far commutativity* `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i - j| ≥ 2`.\n\nThe bar involution `* : H_n(q) → H_n(q)` is the antilinear\nextension of `σ_i ↦ σ_i⁻¹`, `q ↦ q⁻¹`. The Markov trace is the\nunique linear functional `tr_M : H_n(q) → R` invariant under\nMarkov moves (stabilisation + conjugation).\n\nThis is a placeholder structure pending Mathlib's eventual\nformalisation. The opaque type carries enough hypotheses to\nstate and prove the structural results we need, but concrete\nconstruction is deferred. ","signatureChunk":0}]}